{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a \"Fibonacci\" sequence of numbers, each term beginning with the third, is the sum of the previous two terms. The first number in such a sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the eighth term in the sequence?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb081e94e5c63da1ea3844769001ab054d9b298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 34 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 36 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 107 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 152 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 245$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"405\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\